<h1>Gap Highlighter</h1>

<p>
    The Gap Highlighter tool analyzes a policy and creates a concise coverage gap report that you can use in emails, proposals, or client conversations. It identifies what coverages are present, what's missing, and helps you frame upsell opportunities with clear, professional bullet points.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the Gap Highlighter tool showing a policy being analyzed, with the resulting gap report displayed. Show the report with coverage statuses (In Place/Missing) and recommendations highlighted. Include the markdown output ready to copy. -->

<h2>What the Gap Highlighter Does</h2>

<p>
    The Gap Highlighter tool:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Analyzes coverage</strong> – Reviews the policy to identify which coverages are present and which are missing</li>
    <li><strong>Lists in-force policies</strong> – Shows all active policies for the client to provide context</li>
    <li><strong>Identifies gaps</strong> – Highlights missing coverages that might be important for the client</li>
    <li><strong>Shows recent documents</strong> – Lists documents that have been reviewed as part of the analysis</li>
    <li><strong>Generates markdown report</strong> – Creates a formatted report you can copy and paste anywhere</li>
    <li><strong>Customizable recommendations</strong> – Lets you select which gaps to include in the final report</li>
</ul>

