<h2>Using the Gap Highlighter</h2>

<p>
    To create a gap report:
</p>

<ol>
    <li><strong>Open from a renewal</strong> – Launch the Gap Highlighter from a renewal page so it automatically loads the correct policy details</li>
    <li><strong>Review the analysis</strong> – The tool automatically analyzes the policy and shows:
        <ul>
            <li>Current coverage snapshot (what's in place, what's missing)</li>
            <li>In-force policies for context</li>
            <li>Coverage gap recommendations</li>
            <li>Recent documents reviewed</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Select gaps to highlight</strong> – Check the boxes next to the coverage gaps you want to include in your report</li>
    <li><strong>Generate the report</strong> – Click to generate the markdown report</li>
    <li><strong>Copy and use</strong> – Copy the markdown text and paste it into:
        <ul>
            <li>Email messages to clients</li>
            <li>Proposal documents</li>
            <li>Chat conversations</li>
            <li>Renewal review notes</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ol>

