<h2>Understanding Coverage Status</h2>

<p>
    The tool categorizes each coverage type as either:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>In Place</strong> – The coverage exists on the policy with details shown</li>
    <li><strong>Missing</strong> – The coverage is not present on the policy</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Common coverage types analyzed include:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>General Liability</strong> – Commercial general liability coverage</li>
    <li><strong>Commercial Auto</strong> – Vehicle liability and physical damage</li>
    <li><strong>Workers' Compensation</strong> – Employee injury coverage</li>
    <li><strong>Property</strong> – Building and business personal property</li>
    <li><strong>Umbrella / Excess</strong> – Additional liability limits above primary policies</li>
</ul>

