<h2>Coverage Gap Recommendations</h2>

<p>
    The tool suggests coverage gaps based on:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Missing standard coverages</strong> – Common coverages that many businesses need but aren't present</li>
    <li><strong>Document analysis</strong> – Reviews attached documents to identify mentioned coverages that aren't on the policy</li>
    <li><strong>Industry standards</strong> – Suggests coverages typically needed for similar businesses</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Each recommendation includes:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Coverage name</strong> – What coverage is being recommended</li>
    <li><strong>Rationale</strong> – Why this coverage might be important for the client</li>
    <li><strong>Suggested flag</strong> – Some recommendations are pre-selected as particularly important</li>
</ul>

