<h2>The Generated Report</h2>

<p>
    The markdown report includes:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Policy header</strong> – Policy number, client name, effective dates, carrier, and line of coverage</li>
    <li><strong>In-force policies</strong> – List of all active policies for context</li>
    <li><strong>Coverage snapshot</strong> – Table showing each coverage type and its status</li>
    <li><strong>Selected gaps</strong> – The coverage gaps you chose to highlight, with rationale</li>
    <li><strong>Documents reviewed</strong> – List of documents that were analyzed</li>
</ul>

<p>
    The report is formatted in markdown, which means it will render nicely in:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Email clients that support markdown</li>
    <li>Proposal documents</li>
    <li>Chat interfaces</li>
    <li>Documentation systems</li>
</ul>

