<h2>Tips for Effective Gap Reports</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Be selective</strong> – Don't overwhelm clients with every possible gap; focus on the most relevant ones</li>
    <li><strong>Explain the value</strong> – After pasting the report, add a sentence explaining why each gap matters</li>
    <li><strong>Use in context</strong> – Include the report as part of a larger conversation, not as a standalone message</li>
    <li><strong>Follow up</strong> – Use gap reports to start conversations, then follow up with more detailed information</li>
    <li><strong>Keep it professional</strong> – The markdown format ensures the report looks polished and professional</li>
</ul>

